# ===========================================================================
# PCKCIDRT (PCK Cert ID Retrieval Tool) — NOT CONTAINERIZABLE
# ===========================================================================
#
# This component CANNOT be containerized. It must run on bare metal because:
#
# 1. It requires direct access to SGX hardware devices:
#    /dev/sgx_provision, /dev/sgx_enclave
#
# 2. It reads the Platform Manifest from UEFI variables via the BIOS.
#    Containers do not have reliable access to the UEFI variable store.
#
# 3. After retrieving the Platform Manifest, it sets a one-time UEFI bit
#    that prevents the BIOS from presenting the manifest again. This UEFI
#    write requires bare-metal root privilege. An SGX Factory Reset in BIOS
#    is required to re-run the tool.
#
# 4. This is a one-shot operation (run once per host), so there is no
#    operational benefit to containerization.
#
# Install and run it directly on each TDX host:
#
#   sudo dnf install -y sgx-pck-id-retrieval-tool
#   sudo PCKIDRetrievalTool -f host_$(hostnamectl --static).csv
#
# See DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md for the full workflow.
# ===========================================================================
